<section class="not-content awk-sec">
  <div class="sec__head">
    <div class="sec__t"><span class="kicker">01 — What's in the kit</span><h2 class="h2">One kit. Every block snaps in.</h2></div>
    <p class="lead">Each layer is replaceable. Keys live only in the signer; modules talk only to accounts. Pick the blocks your wallet needs and nothing else.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="row__l"><span class="kicker">L0</span><span class="row__n">Signer</span><a class="row__go" href="/concepts/accounts-and-signers/">accounts &amp; signers →</a></div>
    <p class="row__p">The only place a key lives. Modules never touch keys. The same code runs with any signer.</p>
    <div class="row__d"><div class="plain"><span>Local seed</span><span>Imported key</span><span>Hardware wallet</span><span>Safe (multisig)</span><span>MPC</span><span>Backend signer</span></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="row__l"><span class="kicker">L1</span><span class="row__n">Chains</span><a class="row__go" href="/getting-started/packages/#chains">chain packages →</a></div>
    <p class="row__p">build → describe → simulate → sign → broadcast. One seed phrase, one account interface, every chain below.</p>
    <div class="row__d">
